      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Teasdale, Sara, 1884-1933",
      "description": "Postcard pictures of the Keats Parlor and the Girometti Medallion at the John Keats House. Includes envelope. Transcription: 46 Grosvenor St. London W.1 July 24, '27 My darling, this room moved me more than anything else that I have seen. I longed to have you see it too. To-day we drove out the Stoke Poges Church where [Thomas] Gray is buried and about which he wrote his poem. From there we went to Eton and saw the fine old buildings of the college. The boys, dressed for Sunday, were adorable. They are the blue bloods of England, you know. Then we had a hasty glance at Windsor (the apartments were not open and I should have been too tired to go in anyway) and passed Runnymede on our way home. I am loving it all tremendously! I send you many kisses. Sara.",
      "dateCreated": "24 July 1927<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1927-07-24T00:00:00Z/11</div>",
